[/quote]

I had always thought of it as Chicago to Megalopolis as New York.

But, with Megalopolis in Connecticut, that&#39;s obviously not the case...&nbsp;

&nbsp;

In unrelated news, does anyone else get the feeling that our intrepid hosts/creators are starting to hold some cards closer to the chest in advance of OblivAeon?&nbsp; I feel like it&#39;s been a while since we&#39;ve really gotten any&nbsp;<strong><em>big</em></strong> reveals as to the comics canon--the link between La Capitan and Haka is probably the most recent, to my feeling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

But, a lot of the characters that we probably should have seen by now--Tempest, Voss, Miss Information, and Parse, particularly--are still nowhere in sight.&nbsp; And, from what it seems, there&#39;s a lot of major questions hinging on their actions.&nbsp; We&#39;ve gotten every other major character associated with Revocorp, but not Parse.&nbsp; We&#39;ve gotten every core hero (and almost every Prime Warden), but not Tempest.&nbsp; And talk of the Voss invasion has all but disappeared, despite it seeming like a pretty important event series early on in the publishing history, especially given the status of the Maenaryian race, the ultimate fate of Viktor, and the events depicted on Mistbound.

Don&#39;t get me wrong, I&#39;m all for the upcoming episode on Blood Magic and the like, but I can&#39;t help but feel like there&#39;s a bit of &quot;stalling&quot; going on, until OblivAeon hits...
